# Styling

Every public visual component accepts one `class` and a string `style`. Add a class to identify your instance, then target its stable parts. Load the base stylesheet first; see [Themes](/docs/guides/themes) for ready-made appearances.

## Reach elements inside the cropper

Svelte scopes ordinary styles to the component that declares them. Library elements need `:global(...)`, preferably below a local wrapper so the rule affects only this cropper.

```svelte
<div class="avatar-editor">
	<Cropper {src}>
		<CircleStencil class="avatar-stencil" />
	</Cropper>
</div>

<style>
	.avatar-editor :global(.avatar-stencil .advanced-cropper-circle-stencil__overlay) {
		color: rgb(20 30 40 / 65%);
	}

	.avatar-editor :global(.avatar-stencil .advanced-cropper-circle-stencil__preview) {
		border: 2px solid white;
	}
</style>
```

Use `class={['avatar-stencil', busy && 'is-busy']}` for conditional classes and `style="height: 400px"` for inline styles. The shipped themes use selectors, Sass variables and `currentColor`; they do not define a public CSS-variable API.

## Find the right part

| What you want to change | Selector to target below your class |
| --- | --- |
| Cropper boundary | `.advanced-cropper__boundary` |
| Image layer | `.advanced-cropper__background` |
| Image gesture layer | `.advanced-cropper__background-wrapper` |
| Rectangle overlay | `.advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil__overlay` |
| Circle crop outline | `.advanced-cropper-circle-stencil__preview` |
| Handle visual | `.advanced-cropper-simple-handler` |
| Edge visual | `.advanced-cropper-simple-line` |
| Standalone preview image | `.advanced-cropper-preview__image` |

State modifiers such as `.advanced-cropper-rectangle-stencil--moving`, `--resizing` and `--disabled` live on the stencil root. Controls have their own hover, disabled and direction modifiers. See the [complete styling contract](/docs/reference/styling) for exact names and ownership.

## Overlay and crop outline

The overlay shades the outside using `currentColor`; change `color` to change the shade.

<Example source={OverlayColorExampleSource} title="OverlayColorExample">
	<OverlayColorExample />
</Example>

The stencil's `__preview` part marks the selected area. It is separate from the standalone `CropperPreview` component.

<Example source={CustomPreviewExampleSource} title="CustomPreviewExample">
	<CustomPreviewExample />
</Example>

## Controls and nested boxes

Style handle visuals separately from their larger hit targets. Lines draw one border side; set `border-left-width`, `border-top-width`, `border-right-width` or `border-bottom-width` for the corresponding direction instead of adding borders to every side.

If an outer `BoundingBox` contains a cropper, a broad descendant selector also reaches the stencil's box. Use the direct `__lines` and `__handlers` groups to select only the outer controls. The [resizable-container example](/docs/guides/layout-and-lifecycle#reset-versus-refresh) shows that pattern.

When markup must change, provide `handler` or `line` snippets on the stencil. Forward the snippet props so positioning, disabled state and native movement events survive:

```svelte
<RectangleStencil>
	{#snippet handler(p)}
		<SimpleHandler {...p} class={[p.class, 'avatar-handle']} />
	{/snippet}
</RectangleStencil>
```

Use [layer snippets](/docs/composition/layers) for wrappers and backgrounds, and the [custom stencil tutorial](/docs/tutorials/custom-stencil) for a different interaction model.
